<h4>B. The Oil of the Sick</h4>
<p>Research: When is the Chrism Mass celebrated in your diocese? At this Mass, the bishop consecrates the oil that will be used for the Anointing of the Sick throughout the year. Write here the name of your bishop and the date of the next Chrism Mass. If you don't know, search online or ask at your parish.</p>
<p style="margin-top:12px">Bishop of my diocese: ___________</p>
<p>Date of the Chrism Mass (approximate): ___________</p>
<p>Short prayer for my bishop: ___________</p>

<h4>C. Dialogue with St. Camillus</h4>
<p>Imagine you can speak with St. Camillus de Lellis. He tells you that he hit rock bottom —gambler, violent, fired— before finding Christ in the sick. And then he says: &laquo;Brother, the one who suffers is not alone. In every hospital bed, Christ awaits you.&raquo; What do you reply? Write a short dialogue (8-10 lines) between you and him.</p>
